    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.95rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "0.75rem 0 1rem" }}>
      Yes — with one distinction that matters. Udemy is the <strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>seller of the voucher</strong>, not the exam provider.
      CompTIA owns the certification and Pearson VUE delivers the test. That is why the code is redeemed inside the CompTIA/Pearson VUE checkout, not inside Udemy.
    </p>
    <ul style={{ margin: 0, paddingLeft: "1.2rem", color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.92rem", lineHeight: 1.85 }}>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Who sells it:</strong> Udemy, on udemy.com. The receipt and voucher code come from Udemy.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Who delivers the exam:</strong> Pearson VUE, CompTIA's testing provider. You schedule and reschedule there.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Who issues the certification:</strong> CompTIA. Udemy cannot issue, renew or verify a CompTIA certification.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>How to verify your code:</strong> it appears in My learning → Certifications and is accepted at the CompTIA/Pearson VUE payment step.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 style={{ fontSize: "1rem", margin: "1.5rem 0 0.5rem" }}>Refunds, expiry and transfers</h3>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.92rem", lineHeight: 1.8, margin: 0 }}>
      Udemy vouchers and Retake Assurance are non-refundable and non-transferable. They are valid for at least nine months from purchase, and the expiry date cannot be extended. A voucher is valid only in the country where you bought it.
      If you cancel an exam appointment at least 24 hours before the slot, CompTIA's cancellation policy applies to the appointment; the Udemy voucher itself is not refunded.
    </p>
    <div class="callout" style={{ marginTop: "1.25rem", borderLeftColor: "#c0392b" }}>
      <h3 style={{ margin: "0 0 0.4rem", fontSize: "0.95rem" }}>Red flags</h3>
      <p style={{ margin: 0, color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.88rem", lineHeight: 1.75 }}>A seller who asks for a bank transfer, sends a code by direct message, or offers a price far below CompTIA's retail fee. Vouchers are non-transferable, so a code from a stranger may not work. Buy from the official Udemy page or CompTIA directly.</p>
