<section id="study" style={{ padding: "2rem 1rem 2.5rem" }}>
  <div class="container" style={{ maxWidth: "900px" }}>
    <span class="section-title">Before you book</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading">How to prepare so you don't waste the voucher</h2>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.95rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "0.75rem 0 1rem" }}>
      Most candidates need 6–10 weeks for a single CompTIA exam and 10–16 weeks for A+ (two exams). Use one major course, one practice-exam set scored above 85% twice in a row, and hands-on labs for the objectives that require them.
      Book the voucher in your final study week so the date forces the finish, but leave enough room to reschedule if work intervenes.
    </p>
    <ul style={{ margin: 0, paddingLeft: "1.2rem", color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.92rem", lineHeight: 1.85 }}>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Use the official exam objectives for the current code.</strong> CompTIA publishes domains and weightings for every exam. Study to the code on the voucher, not last year's outline.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Do not book before two clean practice runs.</strong> A voucher is a prepaid attempt, not a diagnostic. Rescheduling is allowed, but the expiry date does not move.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Do the hands-on work.</strong> Security+ and CySA+ reward log-reading and incident-response practice; Network+ and Cloud+ reward subnetting, troubleshooting and cloud-console labs.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>For A+, take Core 1 first, then Core 2.</strong> Do not book both on the same day. The two exams test different objectives, and the second attempt is easier when the first is still fresh.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>For Security+, check the calendar before buying.</strong> If you will sit before June 11, 2027, SY0-701 is fine. If your date could slip past that, study SY0-801 objectives and wait for the new voucher listing.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Match the course to the current code.</strong> CySA+ CS0-004, DataSys+ DS0-002 and Security+ SY0-801 materials are still catching up. Check the course's last-updated date before buying.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

